<item>
            <title>[BOOKKEEPER-999] BookKeeper client can leak threads</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/BOOKKEEPER-999</link>
                <project id="12311293" key="BOOKKEEPER">Bookkeeper</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;The client constructor&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;tt&gt;BookKeeper(ClientConfiguration conf, ZooKeeper zk)&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;in 4.4 and above will create a new NioClientSocketChannelFactory but does not set the ownership of that factory to true so threads are leaked.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This showed up as a failure in BookieRecoveryTest on MacOS where it has a hard coded limit of about 2000 threads in a single process, and this test was going beyond that.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
