                            <comment id="15932780" author="githubbot" created="Mon, 20 Mar 2017 15:04:46 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Github user revans2 commented on the issue:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/bookkeeper/pull/105&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/bookkeeper/pull/105&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    Sorry I took so long to respond.  This kind of fell off my radar for a bit.  &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    @eolivelli  and @jiazhai &lt;br/&gt;
    I am fine with deprecating that constructor but it is not going to be a simple change.  I don&apos;t like deprecating an API and continuing to use it internally.  This constructor is used in a lot of places, 28 by by my count, and some of them are not going to be simple to replace.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    There is no public replacement API, except  &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    ```&lt;br/&gt;
    public BookKeeper(ClientConfiguration conf, ZooKeeper zk, ClientSocketChannelFactory channelFactory)&lt;br/&gt;
    ```&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    which is not used at all, and looks like it too was intended to be an internal API that should be deprecated.  So if I do deprecate it I think I would rather do it on a separate JIRA/pull request.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="15932821" author="githubbot" created="Mon, 20 Mar 2017 15:24:45 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Github user eolivelli commented on the issue:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/bookkeeper/pull/105&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/bookkeeper/pull/105&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    @revans2 &lt;br/&gt;
    I see your point. Let&apos;s create a separate JIRA.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    In general we need to clean up the &quot;public&quot; API, but I think this task will be for 4.6.0, now we need to finish 4.5.0.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
